# Rust / Cargo
/src-tauri/target/
# Cargo.lock is deliberately TRACKED (it used to be ignored here). This crate
# produces a signed, notarized binary that ships to users, so the dependency
# graph has to be pinned: without the lockfile every release resolves fresh,
# a transitive patch release silently changes the artifact being signed, and
# `--locked` is impossible. apps/hermes-universal tracks its lockfile for the
# same reason.

# Vite / build output
/dist/
/dist-ssr/
*.local

# TypeScript build info + tsc emit (we don't ship .js for the
# vite.config.ts; Vite reads it directly via ts-node-style loader).
*.tsbuildinfo
vite.config.d.ts
vite.config.js

# Tauri generated artifacts (regenerated on each build)
/src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Editor
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Node
node_modules/

